    "data": [
        {
            "id": "1",
            "que": "What are the meta tag?",
            "order": [
                "paragraph"
            ],
            "ans": {
                "paragraph": [
                    "Meta tag is used to provide additional important information about a document in a variety of ways. Meta elements are typically used to specify page description, keywords, author of the document, last modified, and other meta information."
                ],
                "list": [],
                "codeblock": {
                    "lang": "",
                    "code": ""
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "2",
            "que": "What is the different between html4 and html5 doctype?",
            "order": [
                "paragraph"
            ],
            "ans": {
                "paragraph": [
                    "The HTML 4 Doctypes describe the root element, and provides two ways (a URL and a code for finding it if you have a local copy) for finding the DTD. but HTML 5 Doctype is a magic string that triggers standards mode in browsers."
                ],
                "list": [],
                "codeblock": {
                    "lang": "",
                    "code": ""
                }
            }
        },
          {
            "id": "3",
            "que": "Different between canvas and svg in html5?",
            "order": [
                "paragraph"
            ],
            "ans": {
                "paragraph": [
                    "The SVG stands for Scalable Vector Graphics, and language for describing 2D graphics.SVG is based on XML, which means that every element is available within the SVG DOM. Canvas are used to draws 2D graphics with the help of JavaScript."
                ],
                "list": [],
                "codeblock": {
                    "lang": "",
                    "code": ""
                }
            }
        },  {
            "id": "4",
            "que": "Difference between \"background-size:cover\" and \"background-size:100%\"?",
            "order": [
                "paragraph"
            ],
            "ans": {
                "paragraph": [
                    "Using background-size:cover, background area is completely covered by the background image, but some parts of the background image may not be in view within the background positioning area. It means some of the image may be cut off where as the 100% background-size will be display complete background-image within the view area."
                ],
                "list": [],
                "codeblock": {
                    "lang": "",
                    "code": ""
                }
            }
        },  {
            "id": "5",
            "que": "What is semantic HTML?",
            "order": [
                "paragraph"
            ],
            "ans": {
                "paragraph": [
                    "Semantic HTML clearly defines what kind of code it is holding and help for structuring and understanding of the layout."
                ],
                "list": [],
                "codeblock": {
                    "lang": "",
                    "code": ""
                }
            }
        },  {
            "id": "6",
            "que": "Why to use HTML5 semantic tag instead of div ?",
            "order": [
                "paragraph"
            ],
            "ans": {
                "paragraph": [
                    "Semantic tags used for proper Separation of content, presentation and understanding of the layout. Using the semantic elements, the name clearly defines what kind of code it is holding. Where as using div tag we have to define a class or id that tells about what kind of code it is holding."
                ],
                "list": [],
                "codeblock": {
                    "lang": "",
                    "code": ""
                }
            }
        },  {
            "id": "7",
            "que": "What is local storage in HTML5?",
            "order": [
                "paragraph"
            ],
            "ans": {
                "paragraph": [
                    "Using local storage, web applications can store data locally within the user's browser. Before HTML5, application data had to be stored in cookies, included in every server request. Local storage is more secure, and large amounts of data(upto 5MB) can be stored locally, without affecting website performance."
                ],
                "list": [],
                "codeblock": {
                    "lang": "",
                    "code": ""
                }
            }
